    <summaries>
      <summary>
        <versionCode>00</versionCode>
        <actionDate>2026-07-09</actionDate>
        <actionDesc>Introduced in House</actionDesc>
        <updateDate>2026-11-05T13:36:45Z</updateDate>
        <text><![CDATA[<p><em>The following analysis is based on <a href="https://docs.house.gov/billsthisweek/20261109/H.R.%209614,%20NRC%20Staff%20Pay%20Alignment%20Act.pdf">draft bill text</a> that was made available by the House of Representatives and may differ from the bill text as introduced.</em></p><p><strong>NRC Staff Pay Alignment Act</strong></p><p>This bill allows the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) to increase the annual compensation of a career appointee. Specifically, NRC may set such compensation at a rate that is up to 10% over the maximum annual rate of basic pay for a Senior Executive Service position within the&nbsp;NRC. This authority applies regardless of when the career appointee was appointed.&nbsp;</p>]]></text>
      </summary>
    </summaries>
